# Commit + push = update web

Live site: **https://learninghub.benedicttsang.uk** (Google Cloud Run via `cloudbuild.yaml`).

When the user asks to **commit and push** (including diff-tab commit-and-push):

1. Commit only the relevant files as usual.
2. **Also update the live website** — do not wait for them to say “update the web / 網頁”.
3. Land the same commit on **`main`** and `git push origin main`.
4. **Pushing `main` alone is not enough** if Cloud Build did not auto-trigger. Also run a production deploy:
   - Prefer: `gcloud builds submit --config cloudbuild.yaml` (from repo root, with gcloud authenticated), **or**
   - Ask the user to open [Google Cloud Build](https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds) → Run / Retry the `learning-hub` trigger for latest `main`.
5. Confirm the site’s `last-modified` / UI changed after deploy (hard refresh).
6. If Edge Function code changed, deploy those too when credentials allow.
7. Never treat feature-branch-only push as “done”.
